    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Five to eight out of a thousand births have congenital heart disease. Some of these defects are minor whereas majority would manifest with such severity, as to need urgent medical attention. Some children who have a heart defect from birth appear cyanosed (blue) at a variable time interval after birth. The cyanosis is more evident when the baby cries. A baby who is blue at birth may have a serious heart disease and may need urgent examination by a doctor and evaluation by a paediatric cardiologist. Such babies also usually need urgent cardiac surgery\", informed Dr Mehnaz Atiq, Consultant Paediatric Cardiologist and Assistant Professor of Paediatrics, The Aga Khan University Hospital. She was giving a presentation on \"Common Heart Diseases in Newborns, Infants and Children\" at 'Signs, Symptoms and Care', monthly health awareness program, held on November 27, 1999.",
